+## Routes
+
+- `POST /import/sales` accepts `{ "csv": "..." }`, with columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty`. `soldAt` includes a timezone; `qty` is a positive
+  whole number of portions. Returns `{ "tickets": 1, "dishes": 2 }`, counting
+  new tickets and total portions imported. Known tickets are skipped. Invalid
+  rows (including rows for known tickets) or insufficient stock reject the
+  whole file with `sales_row`, naming the physical CSV row (header is row 1).
+  Consumption is dated at soldAt, with ref `sale:<ticket>`.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` returns an array of
+  `{ itemId, theoretical, actual, difference }` sorted by itemId. Dates are
+  inclusive UTC days; difference is actual minus theoretical, in item units.
+  Theoretical use uses saved sale ingredients; actual includes all consume
+  movements. Items with neither positive theoretical nor actual use are omitted.
